---
import MissionControlSimulation from "../MissionControlSimulation.jsx";
---

<section id="interactive" class="interactive-section">
  <div class="interactive-shell">
    <header class="interactive-header">
      <p class="section-kicker">Apollo 11 / Mission Control</p>
      <h1 class="section-heading">Mission Control: Handle the 1202 Alarm</h1>
      <hr class="section-rule" />
      <p class="interactive-briefing">
        The Apollo 11 1202 alarm was not a simple system crash. It was a program
        alarm caused by computer overload during the lunar descent. The Apollo
        Guidance Computer had to keep supporting critical landing tasks while
        managing limited processing resources.
      </p>
      <p class="interactive-briefing">
        In this simulation, you act as a Mission Control engineer responding to
        the alarm. Your decisions shape the computer load and the final GO or
        ABORT recommendation.
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="interactive-card interactive-explanation card">
      <h2>What This Shows</h2>
      <p>
        This simulation shows how computer architecture concepts apply in
        real-time systems. During an overload, the key issue is not only raw
        speed, but how the system prioritizes tasks, handles errors, and
        preserves critical operations.
      </p>
      <p>
        The activity connects the Apollo 11 1202 alarm to processor workload,
        task prioritization, real-time execution, and fault recovery.
      </p>
    </article>

    <MissionControlSimulation client:load />

    <div class="interactive-grid">
      <div class="interactive-card how-to-card card">
        <div class="how-to-details">
          <ul>
            <li>
              Review the computer message, mission details, and current system
              status.
            </li>
            <li>
              Choose whether to abort, continue the descent, or check task
              priority.
            </li>
            <li>
              Prioritize the task that should receive processor attention during
              the overload.
            </li>
            <li>
              Monitor how each decision changes the computer load and risk
              level.
            </li>
            <li>
              Use the final system recommendation to decide whether to give a GO
              or ABORT command.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="how-to-divider"></div>

        <div class="how-to-title-wrap">
          <h3>How to<br />Play</h3>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* ── Section shell ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .interactive-section {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    /* override global section { padding: 8% } */
    padding: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem) clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(124, 58, 237, 0.16), transparent 34%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(6, 6, 15, 0.98), rgba(12, 12, 30, 1));
  }

  .interactive-shell {
    width: min(1200px, 90vw);
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
  }

  /* ── Header ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .interactive-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .interactive-header .section-heading {
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .interactive-briefing {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* ── Stacked cards ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .interactive-grid {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  .interactive-card {
    width: 100%;
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
    background: linear-gradient(
      180deg,
      rgba(19, 19, 58, 0.92),
      rgba(16, 16, 42, 0.96)
    );
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--border) 80%, transparent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
  }

  .interactive-card h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
  }

  .interactive-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.1rem;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    list-style: disc;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .interactive-list li {
    padding-left: 0.25rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .interactive-card p + p {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
  }

  /* ── How to Play card ─────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .how-to-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3fr auto 1fr;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    align-items: center;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .how-to-title-wrap {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .how-to-title-wrap h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3.5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .how-to-divider {
    width: 1px;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 60px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text-primary) 45%, transparent);
  }

  .how-to-details {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .how-to-details ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    list-style: disc;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .how-to-details li {
    margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .how-to-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.25rem;
    }

    .how-to-title-wrap {
      justify-content: flex-start;
      text-align: left;
    }

    .how-to-title-wrap h3 {
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 10vw, 3rem);
    }

    .how-to-divider {
      width: 100%;
      height: 1px;
      min-height: 0;
    }
  }

  /* Simulation wrapper — no extra padding, just let the component fill */
  .interactive-card-wide {
    padding: clamp(0.5rem, 1vw, 1rem);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* ── Mobile ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .interactive-section {
      padding: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 5rem) 1rem;
    }

    .interactive-card {
      padding: 1.1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
